:: StoryTitle
The Lighthouse

:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "5B1C6A0E-3F7D-4C8A-9E21-7D4F2B8C1A90",
  "format": "Harlowe",
  "format-version": "3.3.9",
  "start": "The Shore",
  "zoom": 1
}

:: The Shore {"position":"400,100","size":"100,100"}
(set: $matches to 0)
The storm has passed. Across the bay, the old lighthouse is dark for the first time in a hundred years.

[[Row across the bay->The Jetty]]
[[Walk along the cliffs->The Cliffs]]

:: The Cliffs {"position":"650,250","size":"100,100"}
The wind tugs at your coat. Half buried in the grass, you find a tin of (text-style:"shudder")[damp] matches.
(set: $matches to 3)

[[Climb down to the jetty->The Jetty]]

:: The Jetty {"position":"400,400","size":"100,100"}
The boat bumps against the stones. The lighthouse door hangs open.

[[Go inside->The Stairs]]
[[Row home->Home]]

:: The Stairs {"position":"400,600","size":"100,100"}
(transition: "dissolve")[A spiral of iron steps climbs into the dark.]

(if: $matches > 0)[[[Strike a match->The Lamp Room]]](else:)[[[Feel your way up->Lost]]]

:: The Lamp Room {"position":"250,800","size":"100,100"}
The great lamp is cracked, but the wick is dry. You light it, and the beam sweeps out across the water.

(link: "Watch the ships")[(goto: "Dawn")]

:: Lost {"position":"600,800","size":"100,100"}
You climb and climb. Somewhere above you, a door bangs in the wind.

[[Go back down->The Jetty]]

:: Dawn {"position":"250,1000","size":"100,100"}
By morning, three ships have found their way into the harbour. THE END.

:: Home {"position":"700,550","size":"100,100"}
You row home. The lighthouse stays dark. THE END.
